// Falkenrath Gorger ([CR#702.35a] madness; [CR#616.1] the discard-replacement
// window): "Each Vampire creature card you own that isn't on the battlefield has
// madness. The madness cost is equal to its mana cost."
//
// The card static (see `cards/Falkenrath Gorger.ron`) is the printed-text
// model and renders the ability, but the engine gathers conditionally-conferred
// replacement/triggered abilities from predicate-scoped ConferralRules
// (`derive::derived_abilities_of` — the replacement gather + trigger scan), NOT
// from a layer-view `GainAbility` grant. So the FUNCTIONAL conferral — a
// discarded owned off-battlefield Vampire opening its [CR#616.1] window and
// exiling instead ([CR#702.35a]) — rides this rule.
//
// `confer`'s `ManaCostOf(This)` gives each bearer a madness cost equal to its
// OWN mana cost ([CR#118.9]); `This` anchors to the conferred bearer (the
// in-hand Vampire), not to Gorger.
//
// The scope is UNCONDITIONAL over Vampire creature cards off the battlefield:
// a ConferralRule carries no source object, so it can express neither "you own"
// (no "you" to anchor) nor "while a Falkenrath Gorger is on the battlefield" (a
// `Where(..)` scope has no carrier and would fault). This is the conferral
// machinery's documented global-rule limitation; it is acceptable for the canon
// madness coverage this card exists to exercise.
[
    ConferralRule(
        scope: And([Creature, Subtype("Vampire"), Not(InZone(Battlefield))]),
        confer: Ability(Keyword(Madness([ManaCostOf(This)]))),
    ),
]
